 Shaping rewrites the model-facing results of every tool the agent calls (`spotlight.experiment.tools` narrows them). `read`, `bash`, and `eval` shape their own results and the TUI still shows their full output. Every other tool — `grep`, `find`, `glob`, `edit`, `wait`, `task`, `web_search`, MCP and extension tools — is shaped when its call returns, after pi's artifact spill and output notices, as command output: data dumps (JSON and other structured output) compacted, lines already shown collapsed, and the size valve, which keeps the `# dir/` / `## file` headings of the lines it shows; a result of at most ~3,900 characters and under 40 lines passes whole (`stats.short`), except that a run of at least 3 lines already shown collapses to `… [N lines as shown before: read T:A-B]` when the run's text (newlines included) is at least 80 characters longer than that marker. `T` is the read's file for a file read, the run's own artifact for a bash output shaped whole from it, and otherwise a copy saved only when the collapse is applied. The last line of command output is never collapsed (an output that repeats an earlier run but stops short still shows where it stopped); lines the call's `i` intent names collapse like any other, since the agent has them in its context already. A bash output whose long lines the sink cut to `tools.outputMaxColumns` is shaped from its whole artifact, like a spilled one, and its cut may be longer than the sink's preview (see **Savings**). Only text blocks are shaped (images and other blocks stay), a spilled result is shaped whole from the tool's own text (up to 4 MiB), and its card shows the text the model got. Calls a tool or script makes itself (eval's tool bridge, a mounted tool command) are not shaped. A `read` of a URL (`https://`, `pr://`, `issue://`, …) or anything else not printed as file lines is shaped like command output; reads of `local://` (spills paging hidden text back in, and other scratch files), `agent://`, `skill://`, and `rule://`, and other tools' calls whose `path` names one, are left whole, as are reads of Markdown files, of line ranges that all end (`file.ts:120-180`, `:1-10,40-60`, `:-30`), and with `:raw` (`stats.rawReads` in the journal entry). A `;`/`,` path `read` is shaped as one call: each part on its own, as that read alone would be (its file window, `:raw` or bounded range decides for it), with one journal entry and one trace whose original lists each part as a window (`original.windows`); a part is never collapsed as seen against another part of the same list. A result shaping would not shrink in tokens against the full output it read is shown unchanged (`stats.reverted` in its journal entry).
 
